  "Samphire": "Not in SR Legacy under samphire, salicornia, glasswort or sea beans.",
  "Romanesco": "Not in SR Legacy under romanesco, romanesque or broccoflower. It is a cultivar of Brassica oleracea, the same species as the cauliflower and broccoli rows, so it could only be approximated from one of those rather than measured.",
  "Freekeh": "Not in SR Legacy under freekeh, frikeh or farik. It is immature durum wheat, roasted, so it could only be approximated from a durum or bulgur row rather than measured.",
  "Fennel": "In SR Legacy (169385 bulb, raw only) but with no amino acid analysis at all, and raw only, which does not match the cooked-vegetable convention.",
  "Cavolo nero": "Not in SR Legacy under cavolo nero, lacinato, Tuscan or palmifolia. It is a cultivar of the same species as the Kale row already in the table, so it could only be approximated from that rather than measured.",
  "Runner beans": "Not in SR Legacy. It carries snap or green beans, which are Phaseolus vulgaris; the runner bean is P. coccineus, a different species.",
  "Dragon fruit": "Not in SR Legacy under dragon fruit, pitaya or pitahaya.",
  "Bell pepper, orange": "SR Legacy carries sweet peppers raw in green, red and yellow only. All three are in the table; there is no orange row.",
  "Onions, white and red": "SR Legacy has one generic 'Onions, raw' row, which is in the table, plus a 'sweet' variety. It does not separate white, brown or yellow, and red onions.",
